baujat#summary.en:
The coordinates of Baujat's plot (meta's `baujat()`): x = each study's contribution to Q, w (TE - TE.common)^2;
y = its influence on the common estimate, (TE.common - TE.common without it)^2 / seTE.common without it^2.
Equivalent to `meta::baujat()` in R.

metacont#summary.en:
Meta-analysis of continuous outcomes (meta's `metacont()`): sm "MD" (default), "SMD" (Hedges' g with the exact J;
variance 1/n1 + 1/n2 + (1 - (N - 4) / ((N - 2) J^2)) g^2, log 69) or "ROM" (log ratio of means).
Equivalent to `meta::metacont()` in R.
